[0.0, "o", "Investigating REAL data for tenant \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: can i trust our crm data? what is missing or inconsistent in the deals we closed this quarter?\r\n\u001b[2m2026-09-23 19:47:54\u001b[0m [\u001b[33m\u001b[1mwarning  \u001b[0m] \u001b[1mmcp.nothing_admissible        \u001b[0m \u001b[36mlabel\u001b[0m=\u001b[35mposthog\u001b[0m \u001b[36mreason\u001b[0m=\u001b[35m'the server was queried and offered no tool Cortex can admit; every tool must declare readOnlyHint: true'\u001b[0m\r\nRead-only: no write capability exists in the tool registry.\r\nCapabilities available to \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: github, hubspot, posthog, slack\r\n  [  0.1s]          checking what data exists\r\n  [ 12.1s]          found posthog__list_projects\r\n  [ 12.1s]          checking memory for prior context\r\n  [ 21.0s] step 1   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 29.2s] step 1   calling hubspot__closed_won\r\n  [ 29.2s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [ 29.2s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [ 29.2s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [ 29.2s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [ 31.8s] step 1   got hubspot__closed_won (2 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 31.8s] step 1   got hubspot__search (3 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 31.8s] step 1   got hubspot__search (4 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 31.8s] step 1   got hubspot__search (5 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 31.8s] step 1   got hubspot__search (6 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 31.8s] step 2   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 37.0s] step 2   calling hubspot__companies query='\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588'\r\n  [ 37.0s] step 2   calling hubspot__companies query='\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588'\r\n  [ 37.0s] step 2   calling hubspot__activities\r\n  [ 40.6s] step 2   got hubspot__companies (7 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 40.6s] step 2   got hubspot__companies (8 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 40.6s] step 2   got hubspot__activities (9 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 40.6s] step 3   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 42.8s] step 3   calling hubspot__activities\r\n  [ 42.8s] step 3   got read hubspot.companies in full (\u2588\u2588 rows) (9 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 48.2s] step 3   got hubspot__activities (10 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 48.2s] step 4   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 53.6s] step 4   calling hubspot__companies query='\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588'\r\n  [ 53.6s] step 4   got read hubspot.activities in full (\u2588\u2588 rows) (10 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 54.5s] step 4   got hubspot__companies (11 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 54.5s] step 5   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 56.6s] step 5   calling hubspot__companies query='\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588'\r\n  [ 56.6s] step 5   calling hubspot__companies query='\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588'\r\n  [ 57.6s] step 5   got hubspot__companies (12 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 57.6s] step 5   got hubspot__companies (13 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 57.6s] step 6   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 61.7s] step 6   calling hubspot__activities\r\n  [ 61.7s] step 6   calling hubspot__activities\r\n  [ 68.0s] step 6   got hubspot__activities (14 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 68.0s] step 6   got hubspot__activities (15 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 68.0s] step 7   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 90.7s]          drafting the report from 15 observation(s)\r\n  [131.6s]          checking every citation resolves\r\n  [131.7s]          re-reading each claim against its own evidence\r\n  sufficiency gate: skipped, this report asserts no cause (0.0s)\r\n  [143.9s]          writing the report\r\n\r\n==============================================================================\r\nQ: Can I trust our CRM data? What is missing or inconsistent in the deals we closed this quarter?\r\n==============================================================================\r\n\r\nConfidence: low\r\nTook 132s over 7 steps, 43,821 tokens, 15 observations gathered, 14 cited\r\n\r\nANSWER\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  Deal-level required fields (amount, owner, contacts) are complete for all \u2588 Q\u2588 closed-won deals ($\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 total across \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, and \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588), so CRM completeness at the deal-record level is not the problem.  [hubspot.closed_won 7ccf6891, hubspot.search a737f253, hubspot.search 71549c64, hubspot.search 59b16a33]\r\n  The real trust problem is at the company-record layer: two of four deal names ('\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588', '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588') do not match any company record by name, and \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 and \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 each have multiple duplicate/near-duplicate company records.  [hubspot.companies 13b4354b, hubspot.companies 278753cd, hubspot.companies 65d46e55, hubspot.companies 99194a06, hubspot.companies 155adcf7]\r\n\r\nFINDINGS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  Core deal fields are complete for all \u2588 Q\u2588 closed-won deals  (medium)\r\n    - All \u2588 closed-won deals in the window 2026-07-01 to 2026-09-23 (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 $\u2588\u2588k, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 $\u2588\u2588k, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 $\u2588\u2588\u2588k, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 $\u2588\u2588k; total $\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588) have non-null amount, owner, and contact-count fields.  [hubspot.closed_won 7ccf6891, hubspot.search 95958be8]\r\n    - A targeted search for closed-won deals in this window missing amount returned zero matches.  [hubspot.search a737f253]\r\n    - A targeted search for closed-won deals in this window missing an owner returned zero matches.  [hubspot.search 71549c64]\r\n    - A targeted search for closed-won deals in this window missing associated-contact counts returned zero matches.  [hubspot.search 59b16a33]\r\n  Deal names do not match the company records they should correspond to  (medium)\r\n    - The deal named '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' has no company record under that spelling; the correctly-spelled company is '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588', a Luxembourg legal-services firm marked as a customer.  [hubspot.companies 13b4354b, hubspot.companies 278753cd]\r\n    - The deal named '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' (misspelled) corresponds to a company recorded as '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588', domain \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, marked as a customer.  [hubspot.companies 65d46e55]\r\n  Company records for CRM accounts are duplicated and ambiguous, especially for \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 and \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588  (medium)\r\n    - Searching companies for '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' returns \u2588\u2588 matching records, most of which are unrelated organizations (e.g. \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 recurs \u2588 times as separate company records, plus numerous distinct '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588'-named companies), with the actual customer '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588) appearing alongside a second near-duplicate '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' record (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588) marked as a separate lead.  [hubspot.companies 99194a06]\r\n    - Searching companies for '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' returns \u2588 records: the true customer (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588), a near-duplicate lead record (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588) also carrying the same revenue and employee figures, an unrelated \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 ('\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588'), and a fourth record with entirely null name, country, and employee fields.  [hubspot.companies 155adcf7]\r\n  Engagement history is inconsistent across deals of similar size  (medium)\r\n    - The company record for the $\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 closed-won deal shows zero logged engagements (emails, calls, meetings) despite the deal's size.  [hubspot.activities 23b04d7f, hubspot.closed_won 7ccf6891]\r\n\r\nHYPOTHESES TESTED\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  [contradicted] The zero-engagement result for the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 deal's company record means the deal itself lacks a sales trail (a genuine data gap).\r\n      A separate \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 company record (id \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, the one marked lifecycle_stage=customer) shows \u2588\u2588 engagements including weekly syncs and CNDA emails through October. This indicates the closed-won deal is very likely linked to the wrong (or a duplicate) company record rather than reflecting an actual absence of sales activity.\r\n  [contradicted] Deal-name to company-record mismatches (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588/\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588/\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588) are simple spelling variants with no material effect on trust in the data.\r\n      Search for the deal name as entered returns zero company matches in both cases; only a corrected spelling finds the record. This is not cosmetic -- any join, report, or dashboard filtering by deal name against company name would silently drop these two of four closed-won deals (\u2588\u2588% of this quarter's count).\r\n  [contradicted] Required deal-level fields (amount, owner, contact count) are broadly missing across Q\u2588 closed-won deals, i.e. the CRM has a completeness problem at the deal-record level.\r\n      Direct filtered searches for missing amount, owner, and contact-count each returned zero of four deals. The problem in this data is not missing deal fields; it is inconsistent naming and duplication at the company-record level, and possibly-misassociated engagement history.\r\n\r\nRECOMMENDATIONS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  P\u2588 Deduplicate and canonicalize company records for \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 and \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 (and audit for the same pattern tenant-wide), merging near-duplicate leads into the single customer record.\r\n      why: \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 and \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 each have multiple company records under variant domains/names, one of which is disconnected from the deal's engagement history, which risks understating account activity and misdirecting future outreach.\r\n      [hubspot.companies 99194a06, hubspot.companies 155adcf7]\r\n  P\u2588 Correct the deal names for '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' and '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588' to match their associated company records exactly, and add a validation check that flags deals whose name has no matching company on save.\r\n      why: Half of this quarter's closed-won deals have deal names that do not match any company record by search, which would break any report or join keyed on name matching.\r\n      [hubspot.companies 13b4354b, hubspot.companies 65d46e55]\r\n  P\u2588 Verify which company record is actually associated with the $\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 closed-won deal, and re-link it to the customer-lifecycle-stage record with the \u2588\u2588 logged engagements if it is currently linked to the empty one.\r\n      why: A $\u2588\u2588\u2588k deal showing zero engagements is inconsistent with a same-account record showing \u2588\u2588 engagements including CNDA and weekly-sync activity, suggesting a broken association rather than an actual lack of sales activity.\r\n      [hubspot.activities 23b04d7f, hubspot.activities 4f29fba6]\r\n\r\nRISKS AND CAVEATS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - Two hubspot.activities observations for \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 (id \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588) and \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 (id \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588) were fetched but seen only as computed digests, not read row-by-row; conclusions about their engagement timelines rely on aggregate counts and commonest-value clusters rather than individual verified records.\r\n  - The \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 company-name search returned only \u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588 total matching records before being read in full; the duplicate/near-duplicate pattern described is confirmed for the read set but the remaining \u2588\u2588 unread records were never fetched at all and could contain further duplicates or the 'true' record under a different name.\r\n  - This investigation checked only the \u2588 deals closed-won in the Q\u2588 window; it did not sample deals in other stages or other quarters, so the naming-mismatch and duplication patterns found here may or may not generalize CRM-wide.\r\n  - \u2588 claim(s) were removed because an independent check found the cited evidence did not support them. Treat the remaining conclusions with corresponding caution.\r\n  - \u2588 claim(s) go beyond their evidence and are retained with reduced confidence rather than removed, because the rest of each one holds. What the check found:\r\n- findings[2].claims[0]: The truncated payload shows \u2588\u2588 total matching, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588/\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 as customer, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588/\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 as lead, and numerous unrelated '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588'-named companies, but there is no '\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\r\n\r\nDATA QUALITY\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - Two activity observations (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 id \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 id \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588) were retrieved as \u2588\u2588-row digests only and not read in full; findings drawn from them rely on aggregated counts, not verified individual records.\r\n  - The \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 company search returned \u2588\u2588 total matches but only \u2588\u2588 were surfaced by the tool and read; the remaining \u2588\u2588 were not retrieved.\r\n  - The github commits sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github deployments sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github issues sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github links sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The posthog annotations sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The posthog events sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - \u2588 of the \u2588\u2588 cited observation(s) returned no results (hubspot.activities, hubspot.companies). Conclusions resting on them describe what was not found, which is not the same as what does not exist.\r\n\r\nSOURCES\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  23b04d7f  hubspot.activities  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/companies/\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588/engagements\r\n  58055faf  hubspot.activities  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/companies/\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588/engagements\r\n  4f29fba6  hubspot.activities  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/companies/\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588/engagements\r\n  0cd4768e  hubspot.activities  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/companies/\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588/engagements\r\n  7ccf6891  hubspot.closed_won  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?closed_won=2026-07-01..2026-09-23\r\n  99194a06  hubspot.companies  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/companies/search?q=\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\r\n  155adcf7  hubspot.companies  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/companies/search?q=\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\r\n  13b4354b  hubspot.companies  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/companies/search?q=\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\r\n  278753cd  hubspot.companies  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/companies/search?q=\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\r\n  65d46e55  hubspot.companies  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/companies/search?q=\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\r\n  95958be8  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?closedate=2026-07-01..2026-09-23&hs_is_closed_won=true\r\n  a737f253  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?!amount?&closedate=2026-07-01..2026-09-23&hs_is_closed_won=true\r\n  71549c64  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?!hubspot_owner_id?&closedate=2026-07-01..2026-09-23&hs_is_closed_won=true\r\n  59b16a33  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?!num_associated_contacts?&closedate=2026-07-01..2026-09-23&hs_is_closed_won=true\r\n\r\nphase breakdown (144s wall, 142s measured)\r\n  phase        calls  seconds  share    mean  tokens\r\n  survey           1     12.0    8%    12.0  in 0 out 0\r\n  recall           1      8.9    6%     8.9  in 0 out 0\r\n  loop_model       7     49.9   35%     7.1  in 14 out 3,752 cached 136,601\r\n  loop_tools       6     19.8   14%     3.3  in 0 out 0\r\n  draft            1     40.9   28%    40.9  in 35,698 out 4,357\r\n  gate             1      0.0    0%     0.0  in 0 out 0\r\n  verify           1     10.3    7%    10.3  in 37,207 out 1,269\r\n  sufficiency      1      0.0    0%     0.0  in 0 out 0\r\n  unmeasured              2.0    1%\r\n  cache hit rate: 65%\r\n"]
